---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Note from "../../components/Note.astro";
const title = "polymath — the dysfunctional executives";
---
<BaseLayout {title}>
  <article class="container">
    <h1>polymath</h1>
    <p>a polymath is someone with deep knowledge across multiple fields. rather than drilling down into one narrow specialty, polymaths deliberately cultivate breadth, seeing how ideas in physics apply to economics, or how biology informs design. this approach makes you more creative and adaptable.</p>

    <ul>
      <li>learn fundamentals in several domains, not just your profession</li>
      <li>read widely: history, science, philosophy, art, business</li>
      <li>look for cross-domain patterns: what repeats across different fields?</li>
      <li>bring ideas from one field into problems in another</li>
      <li>cultivate curiosity more than credentials</li>
    </ul>

    <Note variant="try">pick a field unrelated to your work. read one foundational book in it. notice what ideas surprise you or feel familiar.</Note>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
